                <head>40. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>At its meeting at 10 a.m. on April 29, 1961, the National Security Council
                    discussed the Program of Action for Vietnam (see <ref target="#d35">Document
                        35</ref>) and approved paragraphs 3a-3e. The NSC also agreed that the task
                    force should revise the program for further consideration of the Council. (NSC
                    Action No. 2416; Department of State, S/S-NSC Files: Lot 66 D 95) No record of
                    the discussion at the Council meeting has been found.</p>
            </div>
